				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1492,
				12
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Rename application identity to FIDDEE\n\nUpdate the native backend to rebrand the editor from 'Land' to 'FIDDEE'. This involves a comprehensive change of product identifiers, folder names, URI schemes, and application metadata across configuration files and source code.\n\nIn `Info.plist`, update `ProductNameShort`, `ProductNameLong`, `ProductDataFolderName`, and `ProductUrlProtocol` to use 'FIDDEE' and 'fiddee'. Modify `tauri.conf.json` to change the bundle identifier to `fiddee.editor.binary` and the development team to 'FIDDEE'.\n\nUpdate internal references in `Entry.rs`, `Scheme.rs`, `CliParse.rs`, `InitializationData.rs`, and `WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs` to ensure the URI scheme, window titles, and VS Code `productConfiguration` fields correctly reflect the new identity. Adjust `PostHogPlugin/CaptureEvent.rs` to tag telemetry under 'fiddee'. Remove the deprecated `WebkitServer.rs` debug utility.\n\nThis change aligns the binary artifacts and runtime data with the new project branding while maintaining the existing architectural structure.",
			"SHA": "37e1304709590ce001a8ffbb2707cf477074204b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-17T15:45:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1499,
				13
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Migrate domain configuration to land.playform.cloud\n\nReplace all instances of the `editor.land` domain with `land.playform.cloud` across the Mountain native backend. This includes updating the `README.md` documentation, `tauri.conf.json` security policies (CSP), and internal service configurations.\n\nUpdate the `Scheme`, `ServiceRegistry`, and `CertificateManager` modules to reference `code.land.playform.cloud` and `api.land.playform.cloud` as the primary hostnames for local service routing and TLS certificate generation. Align DNS command logic (`DnsCommands`) to resolve the new zone `land.playform.cloud` and its subdomains to `127.0.0.1` for the diagnostic panel.\n\nRefactor unit and integration tests in `certificate_tests.rs` and `service_registry_tests.rs` to assert behavior against the new domain strings, ensuring consistency across the build artifacts and runtime environment.",
			"SHA": "87ada867c668fef848ce561612d365d9baab197f"
		},
